index 98ffb18..8220820 100644
--- a/docs/reports/2026-09-12/ember_status_and_future.tex
+++ b/docs/reports/2026-09-12/ember_status_and_future.tex
@@ -457,6 +457,28 @@ well as the present structure. The
 \doc{docs/PLASMA_OPACITY.md}{plasma-opacity calculations} give the physical
 assumptions and numerical comparisons.
 
+An independent opacity comparison uses the monochromatic Opacity Project
+(OP) data \cite{seaton05}. We mix the element spectra using their tabulated
+ion populations and include collective electron scattering \cite{boercker87}
+and the OP screened free--free correction. At $X=0.1$, $Z=0.02$,
+$T=9.284\times10^4\,\mathrm{K}$ and
+$\rho=0.05337\,\mathrm{g\,cm^{-3}}$, the OP Rosseland mean is
+$1.464\times10^5\,\mathrm{cm^2\,g^{-1}}$, compared with
+$1.497\times10^5\,\mathrm{cm^2\,g^{-1}}$ from TOPS on the same frequency
+mesh, a difference of 2.165\%. The mixture corrections lower the OP mean
+by 1.499\% at this point and by 0.7450\% in an envelope layer of the
+computed star at $T=5.376\times10^4\,\mathrm{K}$ and
+$\rho=0.005500\,\mathrm{g\,cm^{-3}}$.
+These comparisons use four tabulated temperatures and densities for
+interpolation; results from two-point interpolation differ by several percent.
+The OP mixture omits P, Cl, K and Ti, whose combined mass fraction is
+$2.276\times10^{-5}$, and the dense core lies outside its grid.
+The screened free--free calculation also assumes classical electrons and an
+ionic Debye screening length. These comparisons do not yet supply an
+alternative opacity family for evolution.
+The \doc{docs/OPACITY_ALTERNATIVES.md}{OP comparison} gives the source
+conventions, numerical checks and remaining physical limits.
+
 \subsection{Condensates and a hydrogen-free atmosphere}
 The current evolving atmosphere uses gas-only opacity. Independent chemistry
 checks found no condensates in the tested 3000--3200 K atmospheres, but found
@@ -647,6 +669,20 @@ in the conductivity used on the plotted stellar track.
 The \doc{docs/DIFFUSION_ELECTRON_HEAT.md}{electron heat-transport calculation}
 gives the equations, independent checks and remaining physical requirements.
 
+We also evaluate electron--electron scattering in the screened Born
+approximation, including exchange of the two outgoing electrons and the
+occupation factors that enforce Pauli blocking. The calculation retains ten
+electron energy modes and passes independent classical normalization,
+momentum-conservation and integration checks. For fixed hydrogen ions at
+three sampled interior conditions, adding these collisions changes the heat
+response to 0.7768, 0.5337 and 0.4190 of its full-energy elastic value.
+These ratios describe the specified hydrogen comparison, not the stellar
+H/He mixture. The electron--electron and electron--ion collision matrices
+must be combined with the actual ion abundances before updating the
+provisional diffusion velocities below.
+The \doc{docs/ELECTRON_ELECTRON_COLLISIONS.md}{electron-collision calculation}
+states the normalization and physical approximations.
+
 \begin{samepage}
 The saved structure also gives a direct measure of its temperature gradient.
 Writing $H_P=P/(\rho g)$ for the pressure scale height, with total pressure
@@ -789,6 +825,13 @@ regenerating the bulk physical tables is required for stellar calculations
 from a fresh checkout.
 
